Market Challenges
Complex inspection recipes and qualification requirements can slow the adoption of new AOI systems. Semiconductor manufacturers must validate inspection accuracy, throughput, and compatibility with existing fabrication processes before deploying equipment at scale.

The need for submicron surface-height discrimination also places demanding technical requirements on optical components, measurement algorithms, and system integration.

Market Restraints
High implementation and qualification costs can restrict adoption, particularly among manufacturers with limited capital budgets. Installation, process validation, and integration with existing fab automation systems can increase the total investment required.

Limited supplier readiness and availability of specialized technical support may also affect deployment timelines. Semiconductor facilities require dependable equipment servicing and qualified support throughout the operating lifecycle.

